# The LOCAL image set — built on this box, pulled by tag. For `make deploy-up` / deploy/scripts/up.sh.
#
# 🔴 This is NOT deploy/images.env, and the difference is deliberate.
#
#   images.env         digest-pinned, reproducible, what a CLUSTER applies. Its platform-image digests
#                      are placeholders the release pipeline replaces at publish, so it cannot be used
#                      to stand anything up before a release exists.
#   .env.images.local  tags, resolvable today, what a SINGLE HOST builds and runs right now.
#
# The three platform images are built from this repository (docker-compose.platform.build.yml and the
# admin-console unit carry the `build:` stanzas). The names below exist to satisfy the base file's
# `${..._IMAGE:?}` form: compose interpolates the base BEFORE an override replaces the `image:` key, so
# a build override alone is not enough — without this file `up` fails with "required variable
# AGENTD_IMAGE is missing a value" even though nothing needs to be pulled. That is not a hypothetical;
# it is what the previously-documented local-build path actually did.
#
# The store images are pinned to MINOR tags rather than digests on purpose: a digest here would have to
# be re-cut by hand on every base-image CVE, on a path whose whole point is that it works today with no
# registry ceremony. Reproducibility is images.env's job, and the cluster is where it is load-bearing.

# ── Built here, from this checkout ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AGENTD_IMAGE=heros-agentd:local
CONSOLE_IMAGE=heros-console:local
ADMIN_CONSOLE_IMAGE=heros-admin-console:local

# ── Backing stores, pulled by tag ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:16-alpine
OBJECT_STORE_IMAGE=minio/minio:latest
QUEUE_IMAGE=nats:2.10-alpine
VECTOR_STORE_IMAGE=qdrant/qdrant:v1.11.3
GRAPH_STORE_IMAGE=neo4j:5-community
